{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:43:57.687Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-slack-5icn"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The isMainInvocation entry guard swallowed realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, causing npm run docstring to exit 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release gate reporting success without doing its job. Propagate the throw instead so a broken environment fails loudly."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["docstrings","gate"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:43:57.687Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:43:57.687Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"79360686db81ec625130c70839131d1770e5535e0e5776fcf225a7cdf365c53f","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:44:01.052Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:44:01.052Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:44:01.052Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Defect: isMainInvocation caught realpathSync ENOENT on argv[1] and returned false, so the top-level selector called the no-op placeholder instead of main. npm run docstring exited 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release check reporting success without doing its job."}]}],"before_hash":"79360686db81ec625130c70839131d1770e5535e0e5776fcf225a7cdf365c53f","after_hash":"fec35faaf5c7cdae9d5990f7670c42b23561b87af3ddb0b4afd0ee5dc1333621"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:44:04.573Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:44:04.573Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Fix: removed the try/catch around realpathSync(entry) so it propagates. Adopted the canonical reference implementation (pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl) from pm-context, replacing the local self-resolution variant. An unresolvable argv[1] means the environment is broken after Node already loaded this file, and a broken environment must not silently satisfy a gate."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:44:04.573Z"}],"before_hash":"fec35faaf5c7cdae9d5990f7670c42b23561b87af3ddb0b4afd0ee5dc1333621","after_hash":"ea8f07b25d48e5bb1546815ed4c716c15b2d7e04d1323b67769a96340cbe9671"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:44:07.195Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:44:07.195Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Verification: npm test passes (72 tests), npm run docstring exits 0 (3 files, 44 declarations), npm run coverage meets thresholds, and node --experimental-strip-types confirms isMainInvocation throws ENOENT on an unresolvable argv[1] instead of returning false."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:44:07.195Z"}],"before_hash":"ea8f07b25d48e5bb1546815ed4c716c15b2d7e04d1323b67769a96340cbe9671","after_hash":"f8cd8eb5ff0b32ceea5bd7e10740592734a9a4d633ce9432a0b4f6dc2eaffa41"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T06:42:29.061Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7525f7064349b35d9826cadf","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T06:42:29.061Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Greptile (P2 on pm-beads) and CodeRabbit (Major on pm-slack) independently flagged the one-sided comparison in isMainInvocation: pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl resolves only argv[1], leaving moduleUrl holding the symlink under --preserve-symlinks. Canonicalising both sides through realpathSync fixes it. Verified by measurement: with moduleUrl holding the symlink path, both-sides (new) returns true while one-sided (old) returns false."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:42:29.061Z"}],"before_hash":"f8cd8eb5ff0b32ceea5bd7e10740592734a9a4d633ce9432a0b4f6dc2eaffa41","after_hash":"ec590bf78caa61ca69b4707100b2545d7d8e8637ad927d18507e0759702c2270"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T07:18:33.523Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"1684e74de48dd9cf0e628b6d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T07:18:33.523Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"The previous symlink test (isMainInvocation resolves a symlinked entry path to the real module URL) passed argv[1] as the link and moduleUrl as the REAL path, which the old one-sided comparison pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl also satisfied — it could not distinguish the fixed implementation from the broken one. Added a new test (canonicalizes a symlinked moduleUrl, as --preserve-symlinks produces) that puts the symlink in moduleUrl (pathToFileURL(link).href), which is what Node records in import.meta.url under --preserve-symlinks. Verified by measurement: reverting to the old one-sided comparison makes the new test fail (fail 1), restoring the canonicalization makes it pass (fail 0). The existing symlink test is retained because argv[1] arriving through an npm bin shim is a separate real case."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T07:18:33.523Z"}],"before_hash":"ec590bf78caa61ca69b4707100b2545d7d8e8637ad927d18507e0759702c2270","after_hash":"ddd2755b964d13d7d002d5ed6acfdf192e3ff402028c92af5ebd586b091b7f53"}
